====9th====
[[File:Seth-Dormer-Pool.png|thumb|250px|Dormer is saved from freezing to death in a swimming pool]]
*'''[[Freezing Storm Attacks]]''': After a test, [[Callie Hannigan]] visits the [[S.H.I.E.L.D. Academy]] campus pool with [[Seth Dormer]] and another student. Unbeknownst to her, Dormer and [[Donnie Gill]] had planted an invention of their own devising, the [[Atmospheric Moisture Freezing Device]] in the pool to draw Agent Leo Fitz to the Academy. The pool begins to freeze, and the students rush to escape the pool and survive, only just making it out.{{Ref|AoS112}}<ref name="AoS110-112 Placement">''[[The Bridge]]'', ''[[The Magical Place]]'', and ''[[Seeds]]'' all take place some time between the events of ''[[Repairs]]'' on November 23, 2013 (see [[2013]] references) and the events of ''[[T.R.A.C.K.S.]]'' on February 5, 2014 (see other references), with ''The Magical Place'' taking place in the days following ''The Bridge''. The implied passage of time between episodes does not appear to be very long, with each episode appearing to be decently soon after the last. Evenly distributing these few episodes between ''Repairs'' and ''T.R.A.C.K.S.'' ends up placing the events of ''The Bridge'' and ''The Magical Place'' from December 15-19, 2013 and the events of ''Seeds'' from January 9-11, 2014. These dates end up working out quite nicely, as ''The Bridge'' and ''The Magical Place'' avoid occurring on Christmas, which would be strange for characters not to address if that were the case, and in ''Seeds'', during her lecture with Leo Fitz at S.H.I.E.L.D. Academy, Jemma Simmons states, "We tend to forget that these organizations... Hydra, Centipede, A.I.M.... were also made up of extremely brilliant scientists, men and women who started with the same unlimited potential as you or I." The implication from this is that A.I.M., being included in the same sentence as Hydra and Centipede, is openly known to corrupt and compromised, a fact that was exposed during the events of ''[[Iron Man 3]]'', meaning ''Seeds'' would have to occur after December 25, 2013 (see 2013 references). During said episode, Phil Coulson tells Skye that the Massacre in Hunan, which occurred around Spring 1989 (see [[1980s]] references), happened "24 years ago," potentially suggesting the episode occurs in 2013. However, this is impossible, as it has to occur after Christmas 2013 and it cannot be during the final few days of the year due to the term being in session at S.H.I.E.L.D. Academy, forcing the episode into 2014. ''Seeds'' being a few weeks after ''Iron Man 3'' in early to mid-January 2014 also allows enough time between the film and the episode for the aftermath of the film to settle and knowledge regarding A.I.M. to spread, as well as enough time into the term for a test to be given out as mentioned by Seth Dormer and Callie Hannigan early in the episode. Therefore, it must be taken that Coulson is either rounding down from 24.75 years for whatever reason, or is using Skye's thought-to-be age (24).</ref>

