====24th====
*[[Riri Williams]] looks for her welding goggles, asking [[Gary Williams]] for help. She remembers where they are, when Gary says she needs a break. Gary reveals the goggles, so Riri asks for them back. Gary gets Riri to agree to dance to a song together in exchange for the goggles. He plays "Brown Skin Girl," and Riri hesitantly dances with him. Riri slowly gets into it, but she falls back into a table, causing a wrench to hit her on the head. Riri says that it is why she does not do breaks, but Gary says that she was not injured, saying her head is iron. Gary kisses Riri.<ref name="Riri8">In ''[[Karma's a Glitch]]'', Gary Williams says that Riri Williams is "eight years old" when she hits her head with the wrench. With Riri's birth approximated to July 27 2005 (see [[2000s]] references), this scene can therefore be approximated to the midpoint of when she was eight years old, January 24, 2014.</ref>{{Ref|IH105}}
*Gary and Riri label the wrench "Property of Ironhead."<ref name="Riri8"/>{{Ref|IH105}}

===February===
====4th====
*[[Phil Coulson]] meets with [[Luca Russo]] to coordinate a mission against [[Cybertek]].{{Ref|AoS113}}<ref name="AoS113-115 Placement">The events of ''[[T.R.A.C.K.S.]]'', ''[[T.A.H.I.T.I.]]'', and ''[[Yes Men]]'' all take place around the same timeframe, with it being shown and said in ''T.A.H.I.T.I.'' that ''T.R.A.C.K.S.'' was "yesterday" and it seemingly only having been a few days since ''T.A.H.I.T.I.'' when ''Yes Men'' picks up, with Skye still recovering and Jemma Simmons having spent some time taking Skye's blood. In ''[[End of the Beginning]]'', on March 15, 2014 (see other references), Antoine Triplett says that he and John Garrett have been tracking Deathlok for "a few weeks," referring to the time since ''T.A.H.I.T.I.''. A "few" generally refers to a range of about three to five; with the amount of time between the mid-season episodes needing to be spread out as much as possible (see other references), it can be taken that Triplett and Garrett have spent five weeks tracking Deathlok, placing ''T.A.H.I.T.I.'' around early February 2014. During the pre-credits scene of ''T.A.H.I.T.I'', on the day ''Yes Men'' begins, Jimmy Mackenzie says that he and his wife were married "yesterday." A vast majority of weddings tend to occur on Saturdays, so it can be taken that ''Yes Men'' occurs from Sunday, February 9-Tuesday, February 11, 2014, in turn placing ''T.R.A.C.K.S'' around February 5, 2014 and the majority of ''T.A.H.I.T.I.'' around February 5-6, 2014. This works nicely, as in ''T.A.H.I.T.I.'', Simmons says she has only known Skye for "a few months," with it being just under five months since the two first met on September 10, 2013 (see [[2013]] references), and in ''[[Who You Really Are]]'', firmly set in Spring 2015 (see [[2015]] references), Coulson refers to the events of ''Yes Men'' as being "last year," dating the episode to early 2014 as opposed to late 2013.</ref>

