====15th====
*[[Trevor Slattery]] is taken to be killed by the [[Ten Rings (Organization)|Ten Rings]]. Out of fear, he begins reciting ''{{WPS|Macbeth}}''. The Ten Rings are entertained and decide to keep him alive as their entertainer. He begins performing for the organization weekly.{{Ref|SCatLotTR}}<ref name="AHTK Placement"/>
*'''[[Search for the Clairvoyant]]''': [[Phil Coulson]] attends a meeting with [[Jasper Sitwell]], [[Victoria Hand]], [[Felix Blake]], [[John Garrett]] and his [[Garrett's Team|team]] to discuss the possible identities of the [[Clairvoyant]]. Sitwell is later ordered to report to the S.H.I.E.L.D. ship ''[[Lemurian Star]]''.{{Ref|AoS116}}<ref name="CATWS/AoS116-122 Placement">Despite Glenn Talbot saying in ''[[Shadows]]'', set sometime around mid-2014 (see other references), that Coulson and his team managed to evade him and the military for "an entire winter," suggesting that ''[[Captain America: The Winter Soldier]]'' and the latter half of ''[[Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.]]'' [[Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D./Season One|Season One]] take place around late 2013, the majority of the evidence would suggest that they take place around early Spring 2014.<br>
In ''[[Who You Really Are]]'', firmly set in Spring 2015 (see [[2015]] references), Coulson refers to the events of ''[[Yes Men]]'', set before ''The Winter Soldier'', as being "last year." In ''[[Captain America: Civil War]]'', in June 2016 (see [[2016]] references), Sam Wilson tells Steve Rogers that their search for Bucky Barnes following ''The Winter Soldier'' lasted "two years." At the end of ''The Winter Soldier'', it can just barely be seen that Nick Fury's fake gravestone dates his year of death to "[[:File:Gravestone.png|2014]]." In ''[[Inside Voices]]'', set in May 2018 (see [[2018]] references), a flashback to events shortly following the climax of ''[[Beginning of the End]]'' is shown to be "four years ago." Finally, in ''[[Hot Potato Soup]]'', in April 2017 (see [[2017]] references), Daisy Johnson tells Billy Koenig that the two of them have known each other for "three years," after having met at the very end of ''Beginning of the End''. Therefore, this must mean that ''The Winter Soldier'' and the subsequent episodes of ''Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.'' Season One take place in 2014, discrediting a small "[[:File:Batrocsinterrogation.jpg|2013.10.12]]" date that can be seen in the film. Taking into consideration Talbot's line from ''Shadows'', this would initially suggest that the film and the final half of ''Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.'' Season One takes place in January 2014, which would allow for most, but not all, of Winter 2013-2014 to occur after the events of the film. However, ''[[Marvel Studios' The Marvel Cinematic Universe: An Official Timeline]]'' places the events of ''The Winter Soldier'' firmly in "Spring 2014." Additionally, in ''[[End of the Beginning]]'', a [[:File:DeathlokAimingAtMMay.png|March 2014 calendar]] appears in the background during Deathlok's fight with Felix Blake. Finally, Skye's S.H.I.E.L.D. badge, which she is given in ''End of the Beginning'', has an issue date of "[[:File:Skye Level 1 ID.jpg|2014MAR15]]." All of this, together, would suggest that the main events of ''The Winter Soldier'' span March 15-22, 2014 and ''End of the Beginning'' through ''Beginning of the End'' spans March 15-25, 2014. This fits better with the nice weather depicted in the film, which wouldn't work with January 2014, and also fits nicely with Rogers, born July 4, 1918, saying in the film that he is "95," placing the film sometime between July 4, 2013 and July 3, 2014, as well as Scarlett Johansson [https://www.comingsoon.net/movies/news/109633-scarlett-johansson-talks-timeline-of-captain-america-the-winter-soldier saying] that the film is set "in real time," with March 15-22, 2014 being decently close to its real-world April 4, 2014 release date. With a firm March 2014 placement established, Talbot's line must either be discounted, or it must be taken that Talbot is conflating a period of early spring snowfall that may have occurred following the events of Season One (which is not entirely impossible, considering the Providence base's location in Ontario, Canada) as being a part of "winter," and is referring to winter coming to a resolute, "entire" close. Additionally, in the ''[[Black Widow Prelude]]'', security footage of the climax of ''The Winter Soldier'' is dated to "[[:File:BP Prelude - Ross-Hawley.jpg|17:27-04/04/14]]." However, considering the climax of the film occurs during sunrise/morning and not during the evening, it can be taken that this is instead when the footage was obtained or retrieved, allowing March 2014 to still work.</ref>
