====13th====
*Interns at [[Landman and Zack]], [[Matt Murdock]] and [[Foggy Nelson]], listen in on a legal case where [[Parish Landman]] wishes to peruse damages against a factory worker for the [[Roxxon Corporation]] who developed an illness.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DD110 2014 Flashbacks"/> 
*[[File:Nelson v. Murdock 4.jpg|thumb|250px|Nelson and Murdock agree to leave [[Landman and Zack|the firm]]]]In the makeshift office, Nelson and Murdock, soon to receive their law licenses, are offered permanent jobs at the firm. Nelson shows great enthusiasm about the offer, but Murdock believes that working for such a soulless company is not the right direction for them to go in. Murdock manages to convince the skeptical Nelson not to take the job offer and to instead start up [[Nelson and Murdock|their own law firm]] where they can really help innocent people and make a difference to their city.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DD110 2014 Flashbacks">In a flashback in ''[[Nelson v. Murdock]]'', before deciding to stop interning at Landman and Zack, Foggy Nelson tells Matt Murdock that they are being offered permanent jobs at the company. The fact that they are interning indicates that they have yet to acquire their law licenses, but since the company is offering them jobs, they likely are about to acquire them soon. With the pair [https://marvel.propstoreauction.com/lot-details/index/catalog/198/lot/42618?url=%2Fsearch%3Fpage%3D25%26key%3Ddress%26cat%3D3%25252C%26catm%3Dany%26order%3Dtimeleft%26live%3Dyes%26timed%3Dyes%26regular%3Dno%26buynow%3Dno%26makeoffer%3Dno%26xclosed%3Dno%26featured%3Dno%25253F obtaining their licenses on July 20, 2014], it can be approximated that this scene is set about a week prior to this event, on July 13, 2014. In the present, Murdock states that he called the police on his neighbor for domestic abuse "right after" they left Landman and Zack, so this event and Murdock's first act of vigilantism can be placed on July 13, 2014 and July 14, 2014, respectively.</ref>
*That night, Murdock has trouble sleeping due to overhearing his neighbor abusing his crying daughter. Murdock contacts the police to have him arrested, but the man is able to get away with the crime as his wife claims he never committed the crime and his daughter does not reveal the truth.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DD110 2014 Flashbacks"/>

====14th====
*[[File:Nelson v. Murdock 3.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Matt Murdock]] enacts justice as a [[Masked Man|vigilante]]]] Seeing that his neighbor will not face justice, [[Matt Murdock]] dons a black eyeless mask and goes after the man. He manages to find him at the train yard where he works. Murdock severely beats him up and threatens that if he ever touches his daughter again, he would find him and possibly kill him. The man would spend the next month in the hospital, while Murdock would consider more acts of vigilantism.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DD110 2014 Flashbacks"/>
*At [[Josie's Bar]], [[Foggy Nelson]] and [[Matt Murdock]] drink together to celebrate their new law firm, [[Nelson and Murdock]]. Nelson pokes fun at an injury Murdock acquired the night, believing Murdock's cover-up that he got it from tripping and falling. Nelson, in spite of his fear, trusts his best friend and is glad to be founding the firm with him. The pair toast, beginning their partnership.{{Ref|DD110}}

