*[[File:Stick 5.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Stick]] belittles Murdock's lifestyle]]Stick and Murdock go to [[Matt Murdock's Apartment|Murdock's apartment]] and Stick berates Murdock for his life full of luxury and comfort, saying he needs to be a warrior, leading to a brief scuffle. Murdock is able to stop Stick, who applauds his fighting prowess. Stick reminds him of the war against the [[Hand]], and that Murdock needs to be able to kill people to survive. Stick asks for help in killing the [[Black Sky]], since it will hurt [[Wilson Fisk]], Murdock agrees, on the condition he not kill anyone.{{Ref|DD107}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Page goes to [[Elena Cardenas' Apartment]] and helps her with her groceries, and asks Cardenas for more information regarding [[Westmeyer-Holt Contracting]], she shares the description of [[Stewart Schmidt|two]] [[Joseph Pike|men]]. As she leaves, Page is attacked by the two men Cardenas described, Nelson uses a baseball bat to knock out the two men, helping Page to get away.{{Ref|DD107}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*'''[[Attack on Black Sky]]''':
**Murdock and Stick survey the docks where the ship holding the [[Black Sky]] has come to port, noting the high number of men with [[Nobu Yoshioka]].{{Ref|DD107}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
**[[File:Daredevil at the docks.jpg|thumb|250px|The [[Masked Man]] senses the [[Black Sky]]]]The pair split up, with Murdock thinning out the group of men guarding the area. The shipping container is opened, revealing the young boy that is the Black Sky. Stick aims his bow to kill the boy, but Murdock stops this by kicking the arrow before it can kill the boy. With their cover blown, the Japanese open fire on the pair. The boy is placed into a car and driven away as Stick and Murdock fend off the men.{{Ref|DD107}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
**As Murdock fights off the men, Stick catches up to the car and kills the young boy.{{Ref|DD107}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Back at Murdock's apartment, Murdock scolds Stick for attempting to kill the child, but Stick refutes that that was no child, and that his death was necessary, admitting that he killed him while Murdock was fighting Yoshioka's men. Enraged, Murdock kick Stick, and the pair have another brief fight. Stick berates Murdock for his inability to kill, or even to beat a man as old as himself. He yells for Murdock to get up before he is able to defeat his former mentor. The pair catch their breath, and Murdock tells Stick to get out of his city.{{Ref|DD107}} <ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*At the [[New York Bulletin Building]], Page and Nelson meets with [[Ben Urich]], who berates her for telling Nelson the details of their plan, but the pair ultimately decide to fill him in.{{Ref|DD107}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/> 
*As Murdock cleans up the mess left behind by Stick in his apartment, he discovers that Stick had left the bracelet made from the ice cream wrapper he had gifted him [[1995|twenty years prior]], saddening him.{{Ref|DD107}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Stick meets with [[Stone]] and informs him of his success in killing the Black Sky.{{Ref|DD107}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>

====29th====
*[[Wilson Fisk]] wakes up and looks at ''[[Rabbit in a Snowstorm]]'' before going about his morning routine.{{Ref|DD108}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
