====1st====
*In his [[Wilson Fisk's Penthouse|his penthouse]], [[Wilson Fisk]] wakes up and goes about his morning routine.{{Ref|DD108}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Fisk makes an omelet and enjoys the sunrise before getting dressed. Fisk receives a call from [[James Wesley]], informing Fisk of [[Madame Gao]]'s impending arrival.{{Ref|DD108}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:Dd108 2257.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Madame Gao]] meets with [[Wilson Fisk]]]]Gao and Fisk discus business over tea. She brings up [[Nobu Yoshioka]]'s current displeasure, noting that it has added to her feeling that Fisk has gotten sloppy. She tells Fisk to restore order in his organization, or she will have to cut him out. Now alone, Fisk flips the table in rage.{{Ref|DD108}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Concerned, Welsey calls [[Vanessa Marianna]] to comfort Fisk, who has been angry for hours. Fisk expresses his fear in sharing the truth with her, but she urdges him to always be honest. Fisk recounts the [[Murder of Bill Fisk|murder]] of [[Bill Fisk|his father]], and that he wears [[Wilson Fisk's Cufflinks|his father's cufflinks]] as a reminder that he is not cruel for the sake of it, like his father was. Marianna comforts him as he voices his frustration at the city's attempts to stop him, admitting that he will not let them continue.{{Ref|DD108}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:Ben-Urich-Masked-Man-Rain.jpg|thumb|250px|Urich meets the [[Masked Man]]]]While heading to his car, [[Ben Urich]] is approched by the [[Masked Man|Man in the Mask]]. Murdock tells Urich that he was not responsible for the [[Bombing of Hell's Kitchen]], or the [[Chase of Vladimir Ranskahov|shootings]], and reveals that Wilson Fisk is the man responsible. Urich admits that he has never heard of him, and that the public hates the masked man, so the man asks Urich to write an article to change the public's perception and reveal the truth. Urich agrees to do it, due to Page's trust in the masked man, but he says he needs sources.{{Ref|DD108}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>

====2nd====
*Using the information given to him by the [[Masked Man]], [[Ben Urich]] begins drafting a ''[[New York Bulletin]]'' article exposing [[Wilson Fisk]]'s corruption.{{Ref|DD108}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Fisk wakes up and enjoys an omelet, now joined by [[Vanessa Marianna]].{{Ref|DD108}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Marianna helps Fisk get ready, and selects different cufflinks that his [[Wilson Fisk's Cufflinks|usual pair]].{{Ref|DD108}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:WHiH Daredevil.PNG|thumb|250px|[[Wilson Fisk]] unveils the ''[[Better Tomorrow Initiative]]'']]Urich continues to draft his article, but stops to look at Fisk on the tv. [[WHiH World News]] broadcasts Fisk as he tells the people of [[New York City]] that he plans to no longer hide in the shadows, despite the danger the Man in the Mask poses. Fisk slanders the Masked Man, saying that his intimidation and terrorism will not stop him from fighting for the city and doing what he believes is right, announcing his ''[[Better Tomorrow Initiative]]'' and its goals. [[Karen Page]] and [[Foggy Nelson]] both watch the broadcast in horror. Urich deletes his article draft, knowing it has now been made useless. In [[Matt Murdock's Apartment|his apartment]], [[Matt Murdock]] listens to the broadcast, but is enraged by it, swiping his laptop onto the ground in frustration.{{Ref|DD108}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>

====3rd====
*Outside [[Clinton Church]], [[Paul Lantom]] greets [[Matt Murdock]], who takes Lantom up on his offer for coffee.{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Inside, Murdock asks if Lantom believes in the devil. Lantom divulges that he does, sharing a story of a mission trip he participated in during the {{WPS|Rwandan genocide}}, where a [[Gahiji|beloved village elder]] was brutally murdered in cold blood.{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:Ben Urich meets Matt Murdock.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Matt Murdock]] meets [[Ben Urich]]]]At the [[Nelson and Murdock Law Office]], Murdock, [[Karen Page]], [[Foggy Nelson]], and [[Ben Urich]] meet to discuss [[Wilson Fisk]]'s announcement from the day prior, knowing now that it will be nearly impossible to share the truth about him. Urich shares the information about [[Leland Owlsley]] and [[James Wesley]] that the [[Masked Man]] provide him with, but Murdock admits it is simply hearsay, and they need more evidence.{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Wesley informs Fisk that his approval numbers are rising, and that [[Randolph Cherryh]] wishes to have a meeting. Fisk asks for more information on [[Carl Hoffman]], who is currently missing. [[Nobu Yoshioka]] storms in, upset that he has not been given the [[Elena Cardenas' Apartment|city block]] he was promised. Knowing the Masked Man is impeding Fisk's progress, Yoshioka agrees to kill him.{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[Elena Cardenas]] visits Nelson, Murdock, and Page, informing them that Fisk has doubled the offer for her apartment building. They urge her not to take the deal, to which she agrees. Murdock heads to [[Scene Contempo Gallery]] to investigate [[Vanessa Marianna]].{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:MurdockMarianna-Art.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Vanessa Marianna]] meets [[Matt Murdock]]]]At the gallery, Murdock is greeted by Marianna. She helps Murdock choose some art to decorate his apartment, and is introduced to Wilson Fisk. Murdock feigns ignorance, and makes polite small talk with Fisk, but excuses himself and ends the conversation.{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Seeking guidance, Murdock returns to Clinton Church and sits with Father Lantom. Murdock shares that he desires to kill Fisk, but that meeting Marianna has made his desire waiver, which Lantom tells him is a sign, urging Murdock that the darkness of such an act will only spread.{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Cardenas is murdered by [[Junkie Jake]].{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>

====4th====
*[[Matt Murdock]] arrives at the [[Nelson and Murdock Law Office|office]], where he is met by [[Foggy Nelson]] and [[Karen Page]]. Page shares the names of the two men who attacked her outside of [[Elena Cardenas' Apartment]] as [[Stewart Schmidt]], and [[Joseph Pike]], [[Westmeyer-Holt Contracting]] employees, but that both of them have turned up missing. The trio excitedly unwrap a newly made [[Nelson and Murdock]] plaque for the outside of the door, but Page receives a call, informing her that [[Elena Cardenas]] has been murdered.{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:BMahoneyAnnouncesECardenasDeath.jpg|thumb|250px|The trio learn of [[Elena Cardenas]]' death]]At the [[15th Precinct Police Station]], the trio identify the body as Cardenas'. [[Brett Mahoney]] fills them in on the details of her murder. As Nelson and Page comfort each other, Murdock quietly struggles to contain his anger.{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*The trio go to [[Josie's Bar]] to drink and remember Cardenas. On the tv, [[Wilson Fisk]] gives his condolences for Cardenas, feigning sympathy, further worsening the trio's already dour mood. Murdock decides to leave.{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Murdock suits up to search for the killer.{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*The [[Masked Man|Man in the Mask]] eventually finds [[Junkie Jake]] and interrogates him on why he murdered Cardenas. Jake, afraid of the man, tells him that he was paid for the job at a [[Pier 81 Warehouse|warehouse on Pier 81]]. When Murdock leaves.{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Murdock arrives at [[Pier 81]], but learns it was a trap set up by [[Nobu Yoshioka]]. Yoshioka informs the man that he is here to kill him, after their [[Attack on Black Sky|previous encounter]].{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*At Josie's, a now drunk Page tries to comfort Nelson as he cries, upset with how the city continues to fail people.{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*'''[[Duel at Pier 81]]''':
**[[File:Nobu-vs-Daredevil.jpg|thumb|250px|Yoshioka fights the [[Masked Man|Man in the Mask]]]]Yoshioka throws shuriken at Murdock, who deflects them with his [[Wooden Sticks|batons]]. Murdock and Yoshioka furiously attack each other, until Yoshioka unveils his [[Nobu Yoshioka's Kyoketsu-Shoge|kyoketsu-shoge]], and begins swinging it as Murdock runs towards him. Murdock is able to evade several attacks, but is sliced multiple times by Yoshioka's blade. The blade strikes a hanging light, creating sparks before knocking Murdock into a barrel of flammable liquid. Yoshioka admits that his is honored to be the one to kill the Masked Man, before slicing him several more times along his back and torso. Yoshioka drags a bleeding Murdock across the ground, but Murdock is able to rise, and kicks Yoshioka into the liquid. Yoshioka counterattacks and his blade hits another light, creating sparks that ignite the liquid, engulfing him in flames.{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
**Fisk and Wesley arrive, hoping that the two had killed each other, but upon seeing the masked man alive, Fisk admits to the murder of Cardenas. An enraged Murdock attacks Fisk, but his is unable to overpower him in his weakened state, so Fisk leaves him on the ground to be killed by Wesley. However, Murdock is able to escape by jumping out a window.{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:MaskedMan-UnMasking-S1E9.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Foggy Nelson]] discovers the Masked Man]]A nearly dead Murdock manages to get back to [[Matt Murdock's Apartment|his apartment]]. Nelson arrives, wanting to visit his friend, and hearing the commotion, rushes inside, discovering the half-dead Masked Man. Upon removing his mask, Nelson is horrified to discover that his identity is that of Matt Murdock.{{Ref|DD109}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Nelson tries to get Murdock to the hospital, but he calls [[Claire Temple]] upon Murdock's insistence.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>

====5th====
*[[Junkie Jake]] is pushed off a building by [[Wilson Fisk]]'s men.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[Matt Murdock]] wakes up and assess his injuries, shocked to find [[Foggy Nelson]] in the apartment. An upset Nelson demands answers from his lifelong friend.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:FoggyNelson-MiddleFinger.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Foggy Nelson]] expresses his anger over Murdock's double life]]Murdock explains his powers, and Nelson flips him off, asking if he can tell how many fingers he is holding up, which Murdock confirms as just one. Nelson asked if the [[Bombing of Hell's Kitchen]] was his fault, but Murdock says that it was [[Wilson Fisk]], further upsetting Nelson, who wants his friend to be safe. [[Karen Page]] calls, and Nelson begrudgingly covers for Murdock, saying he was hurt in a car accident.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[Madame Gao]] and Fisk meet on a rooftop and discuss [[Nobu Yoshioka]]'s death and Gao's worry that she is next and that Fisk is losing his way.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*At [[Metro-General Hospital]], [[Ben Urich]] visits his wife, [[Doris Urich|Doris]] and the pair share a tender moment together before her memory fails and she forgets the conversation, upsetting Ben. [[Shirley Benson]] gives Ben the unfortunate news that she could not get him the extension.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Nelson looks at Murdock's vigilante suit, questioning how he knows how to fight. Murdock tells his friend about [[Stick]]. Murdock explains how he can sense people's emotions and intentions, which Nelson is disgusted by.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:Ben-Urich-Ellison-Office.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Mitchell Ellison]] visits [[Ben Urich]]]]In his office at the [[New York Bulletin Building]], Urich researches hospice care centers for his wife, but is interrupted by [[Mitchell Ellison]] wanting to check in on him. Ellison offers him an editor job to help him out, and Urich says he will think about it.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Page arrives at [[Nelson and Murdock Law Office|office]] and is surprised to find Urich there. He urges her to be careful and gives him all the evidence he has on Fisk, wanting to retire and lay low for a while due to his wife's condition. Page, tricks Urich into continuing the case by offering to take him to a care center upstate, and Urich agrees to go.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*As they prepare for a fundraiser at the [[Van Lunt Building]], Fisk asks [[Leland Owlsley]] to reassure Gao. After Owlsley questions Fisk he stresses that change is inevitable, and [[Vanessa Marianna]] is here to stay.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*As Murdock gets dressed, [[Brett Mahoney]] calls Nelson and informs him of Junkie Jake's death, noting Nelson's anger, Murdock stresses that the law is not always enough, and that this is why he puts on the mask.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Page and Urich arrive at [[Saint Bénézet Retirement Care]], and upon Page's insistence, Urich looks around despite the price.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Nelson presses his friend, asking for more reasoning. Murdock shares that over the years he tried to ignore the sounds of people who needed help, but that eventually, it came to be too much, and he attacked a man who abused his daughter. Nelson sees though this, believing it is just an excuse to hurt people.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:Karen-Page-WhatDidYourSonDo.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Karen Page]] learns of Fisk's past]]Urich and Page encounter [[Marlene Vistain]], who they discover is Fisk's mother. Urich realizes this was all part of Page's plan, upsetting him, but he plays along with Page and asks Vistain to tell them about her son.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*'''[[Attack on Vanessa Marianna]]''': Fisk gives a speech at the fundraiser, vowing to help those in need as a result of the [[Masked Man]]'s "[[Bombing of Hell's Kitchen|attacks]]." Fisk mingles with the party goers, but the festivities end when several guests fall ill, including Marianna, horrifying Fisk.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Murdock questions if Nelson would have put on the mask if it meant saving [[Elena Cardenas]], angering Nelson. Nelson yells at his friend, who begins crying, that he puts him and Page in danger, as they would be considered accessories to any crimes Murdock does. Crying, Murdock manages to say that the city needs him, but Nelson states that he only needs his friend, before leaving the apartment.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Nelson goes to the office and throws away the name plate, ending he and Murdock's partnership.{{Ref|DD110}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:WilsonFisk-SadWaiting-Hosptial.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Wilson Fisk]] worries for his lover's life]]Fisk rushes Marianna to [[Metro-General Hospital]], scared for her life. The doctors take her into the ER, leaving Fisk in the waiting room.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>

====6th====
*[[Jonathan Pangborn]] is admitted to [[Metro-General Hospital|hospital]] for recovery. He is given treatment three times a week for the next few weeks.{{Ref|DS}}
*The demolition process begins on [[Elena Cardenas' Apartment]] building.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[Karen Page]] visits [[Matt Murdock]], who is recovering in [[Matt Murdock's Apartment|his apartment]]. She questions him on the details of his accident, but he lies to her and refuses to give straight answers. Page informs Murdock on her findings with [[Marlene Vistain]], and [[Wilson Fisk]] [[Murder of Bill Fisk|killing]] [[Bill Fisk|his father]]. Page gifts Murdock a balloon before leaving.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[Foggy Nelson]] wakes up at [[Marci Stahl's Apartment]], upset about the events of yesterday. Stahl tires to console him, but is unsuccessful.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*At [[Metro-General Hospital]], [[James Wesley]] voices his believe that [[Vanessa Marianna]] may have been poisoned by [[Madame Gao]] to [[Leland Owlsley]], who suggests that he thinks it may have been the Japanese. Wesley asks Owlsley to watch the finances of both, and to speak with Gao.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[Claire Temple]] visits Murdock and stiches the wounds he opened, she urges him to take it slower, suggesting he get some armor of some kind. Murdock remembers the armored suit Fisk was wearing [[Duel at Pier 81|when they fought]]. Temple leaves, telling Murdock she is leaving the city for a while, and Murdock tanks her for everything she has done for him.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
