*Wesley comforts a stressed out Fisk, informing him on who he and Owlsley suspect. Fisk tells Wesley to make arrangements to send Marianna away once she has recovered, to protect her.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:The Path of the Righteous.PNG|thumb|250px|[[Paul Lantom]] speaks with Murdock]]Murdock goes to [[Clinton Church]], finding [[Paul Lantom]] there. Lantom questions Murdock's reason for being here, asking if it was the same reason as last time. Murdock admits he did not kill Fisk, and is conflicted on if he should have. Murdock recounts how he believes his powers were part of God's plan for him, that he exists only to stop the bad people of the city, and Lantom agrees its a possibility, but that Murdock should use his calling to thread the path of the righteous.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Back at his apartment, Murdock meditates, remembering his battle with [[Nobu Yoshioka]].{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Murdock, as the [[Masked Man]] hunts down [[Turk Barrett]] and chases him across the rooftops. Upon catching up to him, Berrett agrees to talk without the need for fighting, so Murdock asks him for the person who made Fisk's body armor. Berrett gives up the name [[Melvin Potter]].{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Fisk gets a call from his mother, but ignores it so he can tend to Marianna. Outside the room, Fisk asks Wesley to return his mother's call and see what she needs. Fisk returns to the room and asks to be left alone. Owlsley returns and recounts his conversion with Gao, saying that she did not poison Marianna, before heading home. Wesley calls Fisk's mother, who tells him about her encounter with Ben Urich and Karen Page the night before.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:Melvin-Potter-fights-Daredevil.jpg|thumb|250px|The [[Masked Man]] subdues [[Melvin Potter]]]]'''[[Infiltration into Melvin Potter's Workshop]]''': The Masked Man sneaks into [[Melvin Potter's Workshop]], finding the armored suit material. Potter returns to his shop as Murdock approches him. He questions Potter, but he throws a punch at Murdock, leading to a brief scuffle.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Wesley asks [[Francis]] for his gun, asking him to protect Fisk, before leaving to find Page.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Potter and Murdock continue fighting, until Murdock is able to put Potter in a chokehold and he yields. Potter begins crying, telling the man that Fisk will hurt [[Betsy Beatty]] if he gives up any info. Murdock vows to protect the both of them if Potter helps him with making a protective suit.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Page finds [[Foggy Nelson]] drinking at [[Josie's Bar]]. She decides to join him, berating him for not communicating with her. A discouraged Nelson says that the story about Fisk's father will not hold any water before asking about Murdock. Page asks what happened between them, but he refuses to give any specifics.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*as Urich researches [[Bill Fisk]], Page calls him, to see if he is doing okay and reveal that everything with Nelson and Murdock is falling apart. Urich tells her that she just needs to do what she can, and she thanks him for the advice.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Page is kidnapped by Wesley before she gets to her apartment.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Fisk promises to the sleeping Marianna that the people who did this to her will suffer, and that not even God could stop him.{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:James-Wesley-Killed.jpg|thumb|250px|[[James Wesley]] is killed by Page]]'''[[Kidnapping of Karen Page]]''': Page wakes up in a warehouse, across from Wesley. Wesley reminds her that she signed the NDA, and was supposed to go away, as it was decided she was not a threat and did not not to be killed. Wesley sets a gun on the table to intimidate her, mentioning her visit with [[Marlene Vistain]]. Wesley warns her that Fisk would be very upset to learn about what she had done, but he offers her the chance to live, by using her skills to work for Fisk. Page scoffs at the idea, but Wesley tries to convince her, by waring that he would kill everyone whe cared about, but he is interrupted by a call from Fisk, allowing Page the chance to grab his gun, and shoot him until the clip was empty. Panicked, Page takes the gun and runs .{{Ref|DD111}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Page throws the gun into the river and returns to [[Karen Page's Apartment|her apartment]].{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Overwhelmed, Page drinks to num the pain. She then quickly takes a shower, before falling asleep{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>

====7th====
*In the early hours, [[Karen Page]] wakes up from a nightmare of [[Wilson Fisk/Wesley-Avenging Fisk|Wilson Fisk]] killing her in revenge.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Page heads to the [[Nelson and Murdock Law Office]], trying to get her mind off of what happened, but is unable to. [[Foggy Nelson]] arrives and startles her, apologizing for how the last few days have been. Nelson promises that in spite of he and [[Matt Murdock]]'s falling out, he will continue the [[Wilson Fisk]] case. Page questions him on his opinion regarding the [[Masked Man]], with Nelson replying that he no longer thinks he is a terrorist, before asking Page to call him if she needs anything.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Murdock arrives at the office, also apologizing for his recent behavior. Page admits that she feels like she made a mistake working here, but that he and Nelson are the only good things in her life. Murdock questions if something happened to her, and she says yes, not giving any specifics.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Fisk waits by [[Vanessa Marianna]]'s bedside as she wakes up, asking what happened. Fisk tells her that she was poisoned at the fundraiser, apologizing for putting her in danger, informing her that she will be protected by Fisk's men overseas for a while. Marianna wishes to stay, wanting nothing to separate the pair. Fisk is informed by [[Francis]] that [[James Wesley]] has been murdered.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Fisk, [[Leland Owlsley]], and his men find Wesley's body. Francis informs Fisk that Wesley asked for a gun and a car before heading out on his own, leading to his death, angering Fisk. Fisk sits next to the body of his closest friend, tearfully saying goodbye after dismissing everyone from the room. Fisk checks Wesley's phone and notes that [[Marlene Vistain]] was the last person he called.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*The Masked Man approaches [[Ben Urich]], asking for information on [[Steel Serpent]]. Urich informs the man that [[Madame Gao]] is responsible for its distribution now in the [[Russian Mafia]]'s absence. Thankful for the help, the man tells Urich to watch his back, as Fisk is an animal.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:Marci-Foggy-Josies-Bar.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Foggy Nelson]] seeks [[Marci Stahl]]'s help]]Nelson meets with [[Marci Stahl]] at [[Josie's Bar]], with a request for help. When he mentions Fisk, she tires to leave, as [[Landman and Zack]] is representing him, but Nelson urges her to stay, so she agrees.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Page goes to [[Ben Urich's Apartment]] to inform him that she believes Fisk knows about their visit to his mother. Inside, the pair work on finding a second source for the information Vistain gave them. Page attempts to stress the importance of posting the story now, and Urich says he will see what he can do.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Nelson shares all his information on the Fisk case, and asks Stahl to trust him, and help bring him down and earn her soul back, worried about her career, she is hesitant, but agrees to help.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>

====8th====
*[[Matt Murdock]] heads into the city, using [[Ben Urich]]'s information about [[Steel Serpent]]. He locates one of [[Madame Gao]]'s drug runners and follows them.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Murdock scales the rooftops and follows the car until it arrives at [[Madame Gao's Warehouse]]. From the rooftop, he watches the runner go inside.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[Mitchell Ellison]]'s son has a cello performance at school, and Ellison attends.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Urich arrives at the [[New York Bulletin Building]], looking for Ellison.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[Wilson Fisk]] picks up [[Marlene Vistain|his mother]], and explains to her that [[Saint Bénézet Retirement Care]] is no longer safe, and that he is taker her to live in [[Italy]]. He asks his mother is she remembers [[James Wesley]], and why he called her the other night. She struggles to recall.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[Karen Page]] calls Urich, asking if he has been able to speak with Ellison, he confirms that he hasn't. Murdock calls Page and tells her he will need the day off, and that he is working on something that will help.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:EllisonUrichFaceOff.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Ben Urich]] is fired by [[Mitchell Ellison]]]]Ellison returns to work and Urich hands him the Fisk story. Ellison is very displeased with the story, knowing there is no source and it will only lead to a lawsuit. Urich keeps pushing him to print it, so Ellison suspends him for the week, however, Urich continues, and Ellison retorts that Fisk is spending millions to save the city. Urich questions what Fisk is paying Ellison, which sets him off, so Ellison fires Urich, claiming his stories lately have been shit.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*'''[[Infiltration into Madame Gao's Warehouse]]''': In Gao's warehouse, the guards hear a noise and investigate it, but are defeated by the Masked Man. The man sees all the blind workers, but is interrupted by Gao commanding them all to run towards Murdock.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[Leland Owlsley]] and Fisk discus leads on Wesley's killer. Owlsley suggests the Man in the mask, but Fisk denies this as a possibility, as he does not kill. Fisk gets a call, which forces him away from the conversation.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:DD112-MaskedManConfrontsGao.png|thumb|250px|The [[Masked Man]] confronts [[Madame Gao]]]]The remaining guards begin firing at Murdock, but he manages to incapacitate them, however, the stay bullets hit a barrel of gas, starting a fire. Murdock questions the worker's blindness, but Gao tells her they had faith in something bigger than themsleves, and that he had taken that away. Murdock leaves to save the workers, helping them all to escape the burning building. As the [[NYPD]] arrive, Murdock tries to escape, but [[Brett Mahoney]] puts him under arrest. Murdock pins Mahoney down, and tells him that he did not kill officer [[Christian Blake]], and that he along with other officers are in Fisk's pocket, before letting Mahoney go and running off.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Gao meets with Owlsley, telling him about the Masked Man's infiltration into her heroin production. The pair discus their [[Attack on Vanessa Marianna|attempted murder]] of [[Vanessa Marianna]]. Owlsley questions if she had killed Welsey, and she admits he would never, as Wesley had never wronged her. She then says her goodbyes before returning to [[K'un-Lun|her homeland]].{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Urich goes to [[Metro-General Hospital]] to visit [[Doris Urich|his wife]], he offers to take her to [[Paris]], like they had always talked about. She recognizes that he has a story he wants to tell, but he admits that he was fired. Doris encourages him to write the story on the internet, since he never needed the ''[[New York Bulletin]]''.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Ben Urich calls Page, explaining to her his plan to write a blog exposing Fisk since he was fired from the ''Bulletin''. She wishes him a goodnight before he heads home. Murdock returns to the office, telling Page she should go home. Page questions if the three of them will ever go back to normal. Murdock recalls [[Stick]]'s teachings, saying that you have to push away the people you love in order to succeed, but that he knows that he can't do this alone. He starts breaking down, but is hugged by Page, who says he is not alone.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:Ben Urich is Murdered.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Wilson Fisk]] kills [[Ben Urich]]]]'''[[Murder of Ben Urich]]''': Urich returns to his apartment and begins writing about the Fisk story. However, he soon notices that Fisk had broken into his apartment. Urich demands he leave, but Fisk requests a simple honest conversation. Fisk apologizes for thinking that Urich's days of being relevant were behind him, but that he tries to learn from his mistakes. Before he leaves, he asks if Urich was alone when he met with Vistain, to which Urich replies that he was alone, so Fisk then admits that because of that he is here to kill him. Fisk lunges at Urich and chokes him out, murdering him.{{Ref|DD112}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>

