====13th====
*[[File:BenUrich-Funeral-Silvo.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Ben Urich]] is lowered into his grave]][[Ben Urich]]'s funeral is held, with [[Matt Murdock]], [[Karen Page]], [[Mitchell Ellison]], [[Paul Lantom]], [[M. Caldwell]], [[Silvio]], Ben's wife [[Doris Urich|Doris]], and her nurse [[Norma]] all attending. Everyone looks on as Urich's coffin was lowered into his grave.{{Ref|DD113}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*After the service, Page speaks with Doris, who tells Page about his admiration of her. Page tries to apologize for getting Ben involved with the story, but Doris corrects her, saying Ben never does a story he did not want to do. The pair share a tearful moment mourning Ben before Doris leaves.{{Ref|DD113}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Lantom asks how Murdock is holding up, and he states that he blames himself. Lantom tells him that he shouldn't, before everyone heads home.{{Ref|DD113}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Page and Murdock arrive at the [[Nelson and Murdock Law Office|office]], and Page questions [[Foggy Nelson]]'s absence from the funeral. Page admits that every time she closes her eyes she worries that [[Wilson Fisk]] will find out that she was with Urich at [[Saint Bénézet Retirement Care]]. Murdock promises to protect her, and that Fisk will get what it coming to him soon.{{Ref|DD113}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*At [[Wilson Fisk's Penthouse|his penthouse]], Fisk and [[Vanessa Marianna]] discuss the plan to keep her overseas, with Fisk noting an irregularity in his finances.{{Ref|DD113}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:Owlsley's Last Moments.jpg|thumb|250px|Fisk attack [[Leland Owlsley]]]]'''[[Murder of Leland Owlsley]]''': Fisk meets with [[Leland Owlsley]], who remarks that they need to find a replacement for [[Madame Gao]], now that she has disappeared. Fisk asks Owlsley to look at some irregularities in his finances, knowing Owlsley was responsible. Fisk pins [[James Wesley]]'s death on him, but he denies any involvement, however, Fisk deduces that the [[Attack on Vanessa Marianna]] was done by Owlsley. Owlsley attempts to blackmail Fisk to save himself, stating that [[Carl Hoffman]], who has been working with him, will rat on Fisk if Owlsley doesn't check in every hour, but Fisk ignores this and lashes out, pushing Owlsley down an abandoned elevator shaft, killing him.{{Ref|DD113}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Nelson approches Murdock as he trains at [[Fogwell's Gym]]. Nelson mentions that he figured Murdock would be out wearing the mask, and Murdock states that he was, attempting to see if Ellison was working for Fisk, but was unable to find out for certain. Murdock berates Nelson for missing the funeral, but Nelson says that he was going to go, but was interrupted by [[Marci Stahl]] sending him some documents from [[Landman and Zack]] relating to Fisk. Murodck warns him that Stahl is now in danger, but vows to stop Fisk now. Nelson reminds him of what happened [[Duel at Pier 81|last time]]. Murdock questions how he can stop Fisk, and Nelson reminds him that the law is what they do, adding that he wishes to find a way to move forward. Murdock agrees.{{Ref|DD113}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>

