*A fire occurs in the church of [[Santa Maria de las Flores]] in [[Miami]], [[Florida]]. The entire church burns down, except for a painting which is over 500 years old. This painting has the [[Words of Creation]] etched into its back. The priest of the church decides to organize an event so as to raise funds and rebuild the church.{{Ref|AoS204}}<ref name="AoS2 Stretching"/><ref name="AoS2 Fire Last Month">In ''[[Face My Enemy]]'', the paper states that the fire was "last month." The reasoned date for this paper is January 11, 2015, putting the fire in December 2014.</ref>
*After the completion of [[Operation Cerberus]], [[William Rawlins]] returns to the [[United States]] to continue his work as Deputy Director of Covert Affairs.<ref name="TP1 Kandahar Flashbacks"/>{{Ref|TP108}}
*[[File:Daredevil ep7.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Nelson and Murdock]] meet with Mahoney]][[Matt Murdock]] and [[Foggy Nelson]] meet with [[Brett Mahoney]] at the [[15th Precinct Police Station]] to get information of [[Ben Urich]]'s killer. Mahoney is unsure, but tells the men about his run in with the [[Masked Man]], and that he said the [[NYPD]] is in [[Wilson Fisk]]'s pocket. Officer [[Corbin]] walks by, and Murdock overhears him mention that he is searching for [[Carl Hoffman]], who is in hiding. Mahoney heads back inside, and Murdock tells Nelson that they need to find Hoffman.{{Ref|DD113}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*At the [[Nelson and Murdock Law Office|office]], Murdock, Nelson, and [[Karen Page]] work together on reading through [[Marci Stahl]]'s [[Landman and Zack]] paperwork in order to find information on where [[Leland Owlsley]] is keeping Hoffman, knowing if Hoffman talks, they could bring down Fisk's operation. Page finds a discrepancy in [[Silver & Brent]]'s property holdings, meaning that must be Hoffman's location, so Murdock heads there.{{Ref|DD113}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Fisk answers a phone call from one of his men, informing him that Hoffman had been found, so he orders them to execute him.{{Ref|DD113}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*'''[[Rescue of Carl Hoffman]]''': Inside an abandoned, church, Owlsley's men are attacked by Fisk's officers, leaving Hoffman as the sole survivor. As Hoffman accepts his fate, the Masked Man arrives and subdues the officers, saving him. The man sits with Hoffman, and explains the opportunity at hand. He offers Hoffman's guaranteed safety in return for testifying against Fisk, Hoffman agrees once the man suggests that [[Nelson and Murdock]] would defend him.{{Ref|DD113}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*Hoffman reaches the 15th Precinct and tells Mahoney that he needs to make a statement.{{Ref|DD113}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>
*[[File:Daredevil113 1517-1-.jpg|thumb|250px|[[Carl Hoffman]] testifies]]Nelson, Murdock, and Page represent Hoffman, and ask that he be put in protective custody in exchange for the information he will provide. Hoffman spills all the information he knows, including senator [[Randolph Cherryh]]'s involvement with Fisk's criminal enterprise.{{Ref|DD113}}<ref name="DDS1 Nov-Dec 2014 Placement"/>

